[{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>For each of the following graphs, identify the points of inflection on a copy of the graph and describe the change in concavity at each point of inflection:</p><div class=\"math-table\"><table><tr><td><p><strong>a)</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>b)</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>c)</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/questions/assets/q1a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td><td><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/questions/assets/q1b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td><td><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/questions/assets/q1c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td></tr></table></div>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/solutions/assets/s1a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<p>From convex (concave upwards) to concave (concave downwards)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/solutions/assets/s1b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<p>From concave (concave downwards) to convex (concave upwards)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/solutions/assets/s1c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<p>From convex (concave upwards) to concave (concave downwards) to convex (concave upwards)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Sketch a graph with a single point of inflection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is non-stationary, concave (concave downwards) before <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and convex (concave upwards) after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/solutions/assets/s2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Sketch a graph which has a stationary point which is a minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, a non-stationary point of inflection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a stationary point which is maximum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Label each of the points clearly.</p>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/solutions/assets/s3.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Determine whether each of the curves are convex (concave upwards), concave (concave downwards) or neither at the given point:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3x^3-x^2-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^4+3x^2+x-6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5x^3-x^2+x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3-12x^2+48x-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=27x^2-2x-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=54x-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=0}=-2&lt;0\\ \\therefore\\text{concave (concave downwards) at }x=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=4x^3+6x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=12x^2+6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=1}=18&gt;0\\ \\therefore\\text{convex (concave upwards) at }x=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=15x^2-2x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=30x-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=-1}=-32&lt;0\\ \\therefore\\text{concave (concave downwards) at }x=-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2-24x+48\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=6x-24\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=4}=0\\ \\therefore\\text{neither at }x=4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>The curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^6-3x^5-10x^4+10x^3+45x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>is shown in the graph below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/questions/assets/q5.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find all the points of inflection of the curve.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=6x^5-15x^4-40x^3+30x^2+90x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=30x^4-60x^3-120x^2+60x+90\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Points of inflection when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n30x^4-60x^3-120x^2+60x+90 =0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow30(x^4-2x^3-4x^2+2x+3) =0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow30(x-3)(x-1)(x+1)^2 =0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So possible points of inflection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3,x=1,x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(3)=-135,\\mathrm f(1)=43\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-1)=29\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<div class=\"math-table\"><table><tr><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"+\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"+\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td><td><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"+\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></td></tr></table></div>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\" data-display=\"false\"></span> points of inflection at only <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,43)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-135)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as the second derivative does not change either side of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,29)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (this is known as a point of undulation).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=12x^5-20x^4-50x^3+90x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>is convex (concave upwards). Give your answer in set notation.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=60x^4-80x^3-150x^2+180x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=240x^3-240x^2-300x+180\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Convex (concave upwards) when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n240x^3-240x^2-300x+180 &gt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n4x^3-4x^2-5x+3 &gt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n(2x-1)(2x-3)(x+1) &gt;0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1&lt;x&lt;\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;\\frac32\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,-1&lt;x&lt;\\frac12\\right\\}\\cup\\left\\{x:x\\in\\mathbb R,x&gt;\\frac32\\right\\}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Find the coordinates of the points of inflection for each of the following curves. Determine in each case whether they are stationary or not.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^4+9x^3-15x^2+4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^4+2x^3-2x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=4x^3+27x^2-30x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=12x^2+54x-30\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Point of inflection when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n12x^2+54x-30 =0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow6(2x^2+9x-5)=6(2x-1)(x+5) =0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-5)=-871\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(\\frac12)=\\frac{23}{16}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so points of inflection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-5,-871)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac12,\\frac{23}{16})\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(-5)=325\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so not stationary</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(\\frac12)=-\\frac{31}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so not stationary</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=4x^3+6x^2-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=12x^2+12x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Point of inflection when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n12x^2+12x =0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow12x(x+1) =0\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(0)=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so points of inflection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(0)=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so not stationary</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(-1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so stationary</p>","<p>Non-stat pt of inflection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Stat pt of inflection at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Given that the function</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=2t^3-9t^2+12t-3\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>is used to model the height, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres, of a passenger on a ride over time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2h}{dt^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and state the physical relevance of this point.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}=6t^2-18t+12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2h}{dt^2}=12t-18\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2h}{dt^2}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0=12t-18\\ \\therefore t=1.5\\text{ seconds}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The rate of change in height (vertical velocity) is at its steepest between the local maximum value and the local minimum value when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The value of some shares \u00a3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\" data-display=\"false\"></span> during the first 12 months of the year may be modelled by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=0.25t^3-3.25t^2+10t+20\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of months since the start of the year.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use this model to predict the value of the shares when 12 months have passed.</p></li><li><p>Find when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2V}{dt^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and state its physical relevance.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=0.25\\times12^3-3.25\\times12^2+10\\times12+20\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=104\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>\u00a3104</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dV}{dt}=0.75t^2-6.5t+10\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2V}{dt^2}=1.5t-6.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2h}{dt^2}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0=1.5t-6.5\\ \\therefore t=\\frac{13}3=4.33\\text{ seconds (3 SF)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The rate of change in the value of the shares is at its steepest between the local maximum value and the local minimum value when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4.33\" data-display=\"false\"></span> months.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2x^3+16x^2+43x+38\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>has a single non-stationary point of inflection.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=6x^2+32x+43\\text{ and }\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=12x+32\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Point of inflection when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"12x+32=0\\text{ so }x=-\\frac{32}{12}=-\\frac83\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-\\frac83}=\\frac13\\neq0\\text{ so not stationary.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Only point of inflection is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac83,-\\frac{22}{27})\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q11","number":11,"question":"<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^3+3x^2+3x+2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the coordinates of the single stationary point of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the stationary point is a point of inflection of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence, sketch the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=3x^2+6x+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3(x^2+2x+1)=3(x+1)^2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (repeated stat point)</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-1)=-1+3-3+2=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the only stationary point</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=6x+6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(-1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-1.1}=0.03\\text{ and }\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-0.9}=0.03\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(-1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a stationary point of inflection</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0,y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0,x^3+3x^2+3x+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=(x+2)(x^2+x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/solutions/assets/s11c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q12","number":12,"question":"<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x^2-3x-\\frac1x,\\qquad x\\neq0\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the stationary points of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and determine their nature.</p></li><li><p>Show that there are no non-stationary points of inflection on the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=2x-3+x^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x-3+\\frac1{x^2}=0\\Rightarrow2x^3-3x^2+1=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow(x-1)^2(2x+1)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (repeated stat point) or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1)=1-3-1=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-\\frac12)=\\frac14+\\frac32+2=\\frac{15}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac12,\\frac{15}4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=2-2x^{-3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(0.9)=0.0345679\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(1.1)=0.0264463\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(1,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a stationary point of inflection</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(\\frac12)=1-3+\\frac14=\\frac74&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac12,\\frac{15}4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a minimum</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=2-2x^{-3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> pt of inflection when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-2x^{-3}=0\\Rightarrow2=\\frac2{x^3}\\Rightarrow x^3=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so pt of inflection is at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is already identified as stationary.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q13","number":13,"question":"<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=3x^4-4x^3+2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> only has two stationary points.</p></li><li><p>Show that the two stationary points of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are different types of points.</p></li><li><p>Hence, sketch the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=12x^3-12x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12x^3-12x^2=0\\Rightarrow12x^2(x-1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (repeated stat pt) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(0)=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(1)=3-4+2=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are stationary points.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=36x^2-24x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(0)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(-0.1)=-0.132\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(0.1)=-0.108\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a stationary point of inflection.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(1)=36-24=12&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a minimum</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/solutions/assets/s13c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>For the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x^4+4x^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the stationary points on the curve and determine their type.</p></li><li><p>Find the non-stationary point of inflection.</p></li><li><p>Hence, sketch the curve.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=8x^3+12x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8x^3+12x^2=0\\Rightarrow4x^2(2x+3)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (repeated stat pt) and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac32\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(0)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-\\frac32)=-\\frac{27}8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac32,-\\frac{27}8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are stationary points.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=24x^2+24x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(0)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(-0.1)=0.112\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(0.1)=0.128\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a stationary point of inflection.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(-\\frac32)=18&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac32,-\\frac{27}8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a minimum</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Point of inflection when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"24x^2+24x=0\\Rightarrow24x(x+1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So non-stationary point of inflection is when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(-1)=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> that is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.20/solutions/assets/s14c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^3+ax^2+bx+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>has a single stationary point of inflection at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2+2ax+b\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=6x+2a\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stationary point of inflection:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the same point.</p>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=30+2a=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=-15\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=75-150+b=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=75\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2=125-375+375+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=-123\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-x^3+ax^2+bx+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>has a single stationary point of inflection at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-3x^2+2ax+b\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=-6x+2a\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stationary point of inflection:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the same point.</p>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=-6+2a=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-3+6+b=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6=-1+3-3+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q17","number":17,"question":"<h3>Prerequisite knowledge for Q17--Q18: Differentiation of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ae^{kx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and solving equations involving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></h3><p>Determine whether each of the curves are convex (concave upwards), concave (concave downwards) at the given point.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^x-x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2e^x-e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{2x}+4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{-x}+x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{-x}-x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^x-1\\text{ and }\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=2}=e^2&gt;0\\ \\therefore\\text{convex at }x=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2e^x-2e^{2x}\\text{ and }\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=2e^x-4e^{2x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=0}=2-4=-2&lt;0\\ \\therefore\\text{concave at }x=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2e^{2x}\\text{ and }\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=4e^{2x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=-1}=4e^{-2}&gt;0\\ \\therefore\\text{convex at }x=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-e^{-x}+2x\\text{ and }\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=e^{-x}+2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=-1}=e+2&gt;0\\ \\therefore\\text{convex at }x=-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-e^{-x}-2x\\text{ and }\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=e^{-x}-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=0}=-1&lt;0\\ \\therefore\\text{concave at }x=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q18","number":18,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=e^x-x^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>has a single non-stationary point of inflection.</p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates of this point.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^x-2x\\text{ and }\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=e^x-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Point of inflection when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"e^x-2=0\\Rightarrow e^x=2\\Rightarrow x=\\ln2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-0.1+\\ln2}=0.623380474952\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=0.1+\\ln2}=0.624047475031\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So a point of inflection.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2-(\\ln2)^2\\ \\therefore(\\ln2,2-(\\ln2)^2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q19","number":19,"question":"<h3>Prerequisite knowledge for Q19: Differentiation of Standard Functions</h3><p>Show that there is a single non-stationary point of inflection on the curve</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x+\\sin\\left(\\frac12x\\right),\\qquad0&lt;x\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2+\\ln x,\\qquad x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=1+\\frac12\\cos\\left(\\frac12x\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=-\\frac14\\sin\\left(\\frac12x\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-\\frac14\\sin\\left(\\frac12x\\right)=0\\text{ has solution }x=2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>(in the range <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;x\\leq2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>)</p>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=1+\\frac12\\neq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So there is a single non-stationary point of inflection.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x+\\frac1x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=2-\\frac1{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2-\\frac1{x^2}=0\\Rightarrow2=\\frac1{x^2}\\Rightarrow x^2=\\frac12\\text{ has solution }x=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>(in the range <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>)</p>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2\\times\\frac1{\\sqrt2}+\\sqrt2\\neq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So there is a single non-stationary point of inflection.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.20-q20","number":20,"question":"<h3>Prerequisite knowledge for Q20: Standard Functions and Product Rule</h3><p>The price per litre (in pence), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, from January to June in 2024 is modelled by function</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"P=144+(t-3)e^{0.5t}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of months after 1 January 2024.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>According to the model, find the minimum price of the fuel in this time frame and the month in which it occurs.</p></li><li><p>Show that the curve has no points of inflection and explain what this means in context.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Min when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dP}{dt}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dP}{dt} =0.5(t-3)e^{0.5t}+e^{0.5t}=e^{0.5t}(0.5(t-3)+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =e^{0.5t}(0.5t-0.5)=0.5e^{0.5t}(t-1)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> month</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(1)=144+(1-3)e^{0.5}=140.7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> pence</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Pt of inflection when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2P}{dt^2}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{d^2P}{dt^2} =0.5e^{0.5t}+0.25e^{0.5t}(t-1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =e^{0.5t}(0.5+0.25(t-1))\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =e^{0.5t}(0.5+0.25t-0.25)=e^{0.5t}(0.25+0.25t)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =0.25e^{0.5t}(1+1t)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore t=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is not valid for this model</p>","<p>According to the model, there is no point in the 12 months where there is a change in convexity of the curve. This means that the rate in change in the price of petrol decreases in the first month, before increasing for the remainder of the year.</p>"]}]